<title>USA: No damaging cold in sight for Brazil coffee - WSC.</title>
<headline>No damaging cold in sight for Brazil coffee - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's coffee areas will see scattered showers and thunderstorms over the next couple of days but no damaging cold, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said on Friday.</p>
<p>The forecast calls for scattered light to moderate showers on Friday and Saturday, with 40-50 percent coverage. Low temperatures of 50-64 F are expected.</p>
<p>No major changes are in sight and no damaging cold is forecast from Sunday to Tuesday.</p>
<p>East-central Brazil had showers and thunderstorms of 0.30-1.70 inch in central and northern areas on Thursday, while the south was mostly dry. Highs were 61-79 F.</p>
<p>WSC said conditions remained generally favourable for the trees in Brazil, with more rain continuing to improve soil moisture conditions prior to the normal winter dry season.</p>
<p>However, this wet weather is unfavourable for the harvest, it added.</p>
</text>
